<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Adaptive-icon foreground, drawn as vector so the app carries no bitmap assets at all: minSdk is
     26, which is exactly where adaptive icons arrived, so every supported device can render this and
     there is no need for a mipmap ladder of PNGs.

     The 108x108dp canvas is mandated; only the middle 72x72 is guaranteed visible, because the
     launcher may mask, crop and parallax the rest. Everything meaningful therefore sits between 18
     and 90. The glyph is a wall panel showing a dashboard: an outlined screen with four tiles, which
     is what this app actually is, rather than a letter or a house.

     There is deliberately no stand. The first version had a neck and a foot under the screen, added
     so the icon would read as "a fixed wall panel rather than a tablet or a TV", and it achieved the
     exact opposite: a screen on a neck above a foot is the visual language of a desk monitor, and
     that is what people saw (noted 2026-09-04). A panel actually mounted on a wall has no stand at
     all. What says "tablet" instead is the front camera, the one mark every tablet carries and no
     monitor does, and it is the same dot the device bezel in the store screenshots draws, so the
     icon and the listing images agree about what the object is. Sketches for this decision, and the
     four rejected directions, are in media/google-play/icon-explorations/.

     Removing the stand also left the panel two units above the canvas centre, because the old
     composition was balanced around the stand's foot rather than around the screen. That is 9.5px
     out of place in the 512px listing icon: small enough to read as "something is slightly off"
     without being nameable (noted 2026-09-07). Every path is therefore two units lower than the
     first stand-free draft, and nothing else about the drawing changed.

     Redrawn on 2026-09-23, with the app's Material 3 redesign, in three ways and no more:

       * **The camera sits in the bezel, not on the glass.** It was a mauve dot just inside the
         frame, which is where no tablet has ever put a camera (Juri). It is now a dark dot centred
         on the bezel stroke itself, drawn in the background colour so it reads as a hole in the
         frame, which is what a camera is.
       * **The corners are rounded**, the panel a little more and the tiles from square to 2 units,
         because every card the app draws has a 12 dp corner and the icon was the one square thing
         left in the product.
       * **The colours are the app's own**, read out of KioskTheme's dark palette rather than
         approximated: #c08cff is its accent and #7aa2ff its second accent, the same pair the store
         banner washes the ground with. The ground is the palette's base, in
         res/values/ic_launcher_background.xml. -->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- Panel bezel. Stroked rather than filled so the tiles inside stay legible when a launcher
         shrinks the icon to a status-bar size. The path is the stroke's centreline, so the drawn
         edge spans 24..84 across and 28..80 down: centred on 54,54 in both directions, and inside
         the guaranteed 18..90 square. The bezel is the outermost mark, so it alone decides where
         the glyph sits; measure both spans before changing a coordinate here. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M32,30 L76,30 A6,6 0 0 1 82,36 L82,72 A6,6 0 0 1 76,78 L32,78 A6,6 0 0 1 26,72 L26,36 A6,6 0 0 1 32,30 Z"
        android:strokeColor="#C08CFF"
        android:strokeWidth="4"
        android:fillColor="#00000000" />

    <!-- The front camera: what makes this a tablet and not a monitor. A 2.5-unit hole centred on
         the 4-unit top bezel stroke, in the background colour, so 0.75 of the frame shows above and
         below it. Drawn after the bezel, because it is a hole in the bezel. -->
    <path
        android:pathData="M52.75,30 A1.25,1.25 0 1 1 55.25,30 A1.25,1.25 0 1 1 52.75,30 Z"
        android:fillColor="#1E1E2E" />

    <!-- Dashboard tiles: two rows, wide and narrow alternating, echoing a card layout. Their field
         is 33..75 across and 40..68 down, which leaves 5 either side and 8 above and below inside
         the frame, so the block sits centred in the glass. -->
    <path android:pathData="M35,40 L55,40 A2,2 0 0 1 57,42 L57,50 A2,2 0 0 1 55,52 L35,52 A2,2 0 0 1 33,50 L33,42 A2,2 0 0 1 35,40 Z" android:fillColor="#C08CFF" />
    <path android:pathData="M63,40 L73,40 A2,2 0 0 1 75,42 L75,50 A2,2 0 0 1 73,52 L63,52 A2,2 0 0 1 61,50 L61,42 A2,2 0 0 1 63,40 Z" android:fillColor="#7AA2FF" />
    <path android:pathData="M35,56 L45,56 A2,2 0 0 1 47,58 L47,66 A2,2 0 0 1 45,68 L35,68 A2,2 0 0 1 33,66 L33,58 A2,2 0 0 1 35,56 Z" android:fillColor="#7AA2FF" />
    <path android:pathData="M53,56 L73,56 A2,2 0 0 1 75,58 L75,66 A2,2 0 0 1 73,68 L53,68 A2,2 0 0 1 51,66 L51,58 A2,2 0 0 1 53,56 Z" android:fillColor="#C08CFF" />
</vector>
